<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">University of Helmstedt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1576">1576</a>–<a href="/years/1810">1810</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Academia Julia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The University of Helmstedt was founded in 1576 by Duke Julius of Brunswick-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolfenbuttel">Wolfenbüttel</a> as a Lutheran university, and for a time it was one of the largest in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, known for its theology and humanist learning. Its importance declined in the 18th century, and it was closed in 1810 under the Napoleonic Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westphalia">Westphalia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/university-of-helmstedt.jpg" alt="University of Helmstedt" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Juleum_Helmstedt_Collegium.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
